# WHY THIS RED
#
# The harm was a dispatch that died on `400 Bad Request: {"error":"driver
# configuration is invalid"}` — a message that named neither the field nor the
# adapter — whenever a hermes dispatch set a reasoning effort. The cause was two
# ordinary decisions meeting: `HermesConfig` declared
# `#[serde(default, alias = "effort")] reasoning_effort`, and `api.rs` composed
# the driver config with the same value under BOTH `effort` and
# `reasoning_effort`. Serde then saw one field populated twice and refused the
# whole config with `duplicate field \`reasoning_effort\``, before the dispatch
# owned anything.
#
# A behavioural replay would mean a real hermes acp-stdio dispatch, i.e. a real
# provider and real spend, to observe a failure that is pure local
# deserialization. So the proof drives the production validation path directly —
# `driver_for_mode_harness(mode, harness).validate(config)`, the same call
# `api.rs` makes before it commits a run — with the config `api.rs` composes.
#
# The injection restores both halves: the alias on `HermesConfig`, and the
# message-free 400.

